      "lineNbr": 5647,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-22T20:27:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is global - do we have a mechanism to prevent any random app from clearing the flags?",
      "revId": "18f11096a8476101eddf9e1bbeb067387a205493",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5380c53b_1df36533",
        "filename": "drivers/android/binder.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 5647,
      "author": {
        "id": 1741425
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-22T21:15:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve thought to allow only the first registered process to change it. That\u0027s why you see a REGISTER COMMAND in binder generic netlink. However, the system_server might crash and respawn with a different pid. On the other hand, adding an Android specific permission check is not suitable for a Linux kernel patch.\n\nSo this is actually protected by SELinux, which can prevent any random apps from calling this ioctl.",
      "parentUuid": "a540b0be_b93a2b8b",
      "revId": "18f11096a8476101eddf9e1bbeb067387a205493",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
