      "author": {
        "id": 1741425
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-22T21:15:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In case there\u0027re multiple processes calling the ioctl at the same time, although extremely unlikely. For Android it\u0027s perfectly fine to bypass the lock here but for Linux device driver, I assume this should be protected. What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "80de2f2a_e6c34ddc",
