      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1741425
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-22T21:15:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then the following netlink message will fail to reach the target process. This is how generic netlink works for unicast. Changing it to broadcast to prevent this awkward PID issue. but I don\u0027t think a random process should have access these reports.\n\nPlease see the netlink doc for how this PID is used at https://docs.kernel.org/userspace-api/netlink/intro.html\n\nFortunately, although the PID recycle issue can\u0027t be completely avoided, this should never happen actually. If system_server dies, it will register its new PID again before launching any other user apps.",
      "parentUuid": "3d114cc4_b5179ea7",
      "revId": "18f11096a8476101eddf9e1bbeb067387a205493",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
